### fix(rpc): early 400 for unsupported chain_id query param (#397)

- `681f4c6bc` — an explicit `chain_id` outside `supported_chains` now gets a clean 400 `{"detail": "Unsupported chain_id: <id>"}` from `RequestLoggingMiddleware` before the handler runs; previously only `/rpc/account(s)/{address}` was guarded (RPC-ACCT-UNKNOWN-CHAIN-1) and every other scope-reading route resolved the id into `session_scope`, opened a stray `data/<chain>/chain.db` and died as an unhandled 503 — the ait-hub residual of ~5,100 unhandled-error journal lines on 20–22 Oct. Rejection is counted in `rpc_requests_total`/`rpc_client_errors_total` and logged at debug. Deployed fleet-wide 24 Oct; live replay confirms 400 on list/details/supply.

